+### R29 · OWASP LLM Top 10 as the guard chain's risk vocabulary — `adapt_cleanroom` → Issue #1733
+
+**Evidence trail (probed 2026-10-28):** the official project page `genai.owasp.org/llm-top-10/` (live fetch)
+presents the **2025 Top 10 Risk & Mitigations for LLMs and Gen AI Apps** as the current canonical list:
+LLM01 Prompt Injection, LLM02 Sensitive Information Disclosure, LLM03 Supply Chain, LLM04 Data and Model
+Poisoning, LLM05 Improper Output Handling, LLM06 Excessive Agency, LLM07 System Prompt Leakage, LLM08 Vector
+and Embedding Weaknesses, LLM09 Misinformation, LLM10 Unbounded Consumption (v2025 published 2024-11; official
+translations landed through 2025-07). The GitHub mirror `owasp/www-project-top-10-for-large-language-model-applications`
+carries the commit **"Mark legacy repository and point to 2026 release" (2026-08-05)** — a 2026 refresh exists or
+is imminent, so the mapping must pin the version it cites and expect the successor. The same GenAI Security
+Project shipped the Agent Control Standard (2026-09-01, → R30), a GenAI Red Teaming Manual v1.0 (2026-10-20)
+and an LLM Exploit Generation Guide 2.0 (2026-10-27) — the initiative is actively maintained, CC BY-SA v4.0.
+
+**Why this maps cleanly onto what SupremeAI already runs:** the federation's control surface is unusually
+well-aligned with the 2025 taxonomy — policy HITL (`policy_preview` risk verdicts, `policy_approve`, gated
+`action_*` tools with `overrideRequestId`) addresses LLM06 Excessive Agency; slot architecture (credential
+fingerprinting, fail-closed `slot_suspend`, one-time credentials, `slot_audit_trail`) addresses LLM02/LLM03
+disclosure and supply-chain posture; the semantic cache and Qdrant lanes touch LLM08 Vector/Embedding
+weaknesses. The striking synthesis: **the live Redis quota crisis (#1698) is LLM10 Unbounded Consumption
+executed in production** — a background consumer with no per-tenant command budget burning a hard 500K cap.
+A taxonomy row that names a current P1 incident is the strongest possible argument that the mapping is not
+ceremony.
+
+- **Pros:** one docs file gives every future RFC a shared risk vocabulary (issues can reference "LLM06-style
+  agency" instead of re-deriving threats); the gap column will likely expose LLM07 System Prompt Leakage and
+  LLM09 Misinformation as the least-covered rows — cheap to verify, valuable to know; zero code, zero deps.
+- **Cons:** a taxonomy is only as good as its freshness — the 2026 refresh will require a re-base (tracked in
+  the issue as an explicit follow-up trigger); risk of checkbox theater if rows are marked "covered" without a
+  named control.
+- **Risks:** over-claiming — the mapping must distinguish *enforced* controls (loop-injected invariants, guard
+  chain) from *documented* ones; the CC BY-SA license requires attribution when quoting list text (paraphrase
+  or attribute; no verbatim copy-paste of the PDF).
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no verbatim copying of OWASP content without attribution; no "security theater" claim
+  that a mapping is a control; no modification of the guard chain itself in this lane.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1733](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1733)** (docs-only:
