+### R30 · OWASP Agent Control Standard as declarative vocabulary for the policy chain — `quarantine_eval` → Issue #1739
+
+**Evidence trail (probed 2026-10-28):** `genai.owasp.org/resource/agent-control-standard-acs/` (live fetch)
+announces ACS on **2026-09-01** under the OWASP GenAI Security Project: agents must be *"inspectable, traceable
+and instrumentable"*, and ACS "defines how agent platforms expose middleware hooks and how safety policies can
+be enforced through them, enabling declarative controls that are portable across agent frameworks and enforced
+at runtime." The repo `GenAI-Security-Project/agent-control-standard` probes at **Apache-2.0 (accept tier),
+220 stars / 73 forks, default branch `integration`**, with TypeScript reference implementations
+(`agt-bridge`, `conformance`, OPA-path integration) inside the tree. Maturity is honest-to-say: two months old,
+modest adoption, reference-quality tooling — a standard to *track*, not to bet the guard chain on.
+
+**Why it still earns a lane:** SupremeAI already built the *thing* ACS standardizes — a preview/approve policy
+gate over credential-bound actions, fail-closed slot suspension, and an immutable audit trail. The evaluation
+question is concrete: can the existing chain be *expressed* in ACS's declarative vocabulary, and would that
+buy interoperability (third-party agents arriving with their own ACS-conformant policies) or just a second
+process truth? That is exactly the Spec-Kit-shaped question radar VI's R25 (#1710) taught the board to run as
+a doc-only pilot with per-field adopt/reject.
+
+- **Pros:** a vocabulary pilot costs one docs page; conformance thinking hardens the policy engine's own spec;
+  if ACS gains traction, SupremeAI is already expressive in it; the conformance suite in the repo is a
+  ready-made acceptance-criteria generator for a future `evaluate` verdict.
+- **Cons:** 220 stars + single-org governance = real adoption risk; hooks are TS-first (reference impls), and
+  the federation's control plane is Python; adopting the vocabulary without adopting value drift requires
+  discipline (same conflict class as `/speckit-constitution` vs AGENTS.md in R25).
+- **Risks:** standard churn before 1.0 (`integration` default branch signals pre-release state); license is
+  fine (Apache-2.0) but the *brand* is OWASP's — derivative claims must respect attribution.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no runtime adoption, no new dependency, no rewrite of the policy engine to "ACS-native"
+  shapes; no claim of conformance without the conformance suite actually passing.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1739](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1739)** (doc-only
+  pilot: map `policy_preview`/`policy_approve`/`slot_*` semantics onto ACS hook vocabulary in
+  `docs/security/ACS_VOCABULARY_PILOT.md`; per-field adopt/reject; explicit exit criteria → promote to
+  `evaluate` with conformance target, or file as `reject` with reasons).
